          "settings": {
            "title": "A ritual you already know",
            "body": "<p>Nothing new to learn. You fill the cup the way you have always filled a bowl: your own tobacco, fluffed and airy or pressed and dense, a mesh on top.<\/p><p>No pods and no cartridges: any brand, any cut you like. The same hands and the same habit, only the coal is gone.<\/p>"
          }
        },
        "item_3": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Why the charcoal had to go",
            "body": "<p>Coal is the one part of the evening nobody loves. Ten minutes over a burner, tongs, ash on the table, the smell of coal in the room, and a burnt edge on the flavour whenever a piece sits too long.<\/p><p>ENSŌ replaces it with electric heat set to the degree. The blend warms evenly and never meets a flame, so what you taste is the tobacco you chose.<\/p>"
          }
